lan(root)`. Print the count. If the fresh set is empty, say so and write nothing.\n- Status model: add `superseded` to STATUSES; add it as a legal move from proposed, todo, ready and blocked; terminal like cancelled/done (no exits). Do not let running/review reach it. Keep every existing status behavior and validation intact.\n- Do not create a scope change order and do not touch the scope approval state; this is a ticket-ledger owner action, journaled in tickets.log.\n\nTests: create tests/tickets-supersede.test.mjs covering: dry-run lists and writes nothing (ledger and log unchanged); --yes only changes stale active tickets and leaves running/review/done/cancelled alone; log-based last touch vs ledger-created fallback; agent session refused without SWARM_OWNER, allowed with SWARM_OWNER=1; invalid/missing --before refused; superseded is terminal and counted in ledgerStats; one appendLog event with the count. Reuse the fixture/helpers style in tests/scope-commands.test.mjs (read it).\n\nVerify: node --import ./tests/_isolate-config.mjs --test tests/scope-commands.test.mjs tests/tickets-supersede.test.mjs -> all pass. Report exact commands and counts.",
